---
source: xtask/src/help.rs
expression: help_for(&path)
---
Release-build the Windows binaries (with --msi, the installer package) or the Linux server, with symbols and size reports, as CI does (docs/packaging.md)

Usage: cargo xtask dist [OPTIONS]
       cargo xtask dist <COMMAND>

Commands:
  driver  Explain how the optional kernel driver is packaged (local-only, #8)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --target <triple>
          The target triple (default: this machine's)

      --msi
          Also build and validate the installer package (Windows targets)

      --sign <signer>
          Sign the executables and package with this signer

      --out <dir>
          Where to write the output

      --bump-patch
          Build as the next patch version (the package upgrade test)

      --compare-sizes <sizes.json>
          Warn about size changes against this earlier size report

      --from <dir>
          Package these prebuilt (and signed) executables instead of building them (needs --msi)

      --no-timestamp
          Sign without a timestamp server (the CI test of the signing path only)

  -h, --help
          Print help
